<h2>STRATOS Voice and your data</h2>
<p>STRATOS Voice records meetings, transcribes them locally and lets you read saved records. Recording and transcription do not require an account. AI text review is optional. You can select your own OpenAI, Claude or Perplexity API account, a compatible enterprise server or your organisation’s STRATOS connection.</p>
<h2>Recordings and local transcripts</h2>
<p>Audio, local transcripts, speaker labels, corrections and your dictionary are stored in the app’s private space on your iPhone. Recording, speech recognition and speaker separation run locally. Some models require an initial internet download; downloading a model does not send your recording.</p>
<p>The app protects records using iOS facilities and excludes them from system backup. You can delete a record in the library. Uninstalling the app removes its local data, but does not remove copies you previously exported or data already sent to an organisational service.</p>
<h2>Sharing</h2>
<p>You share text or audio through an explicit action in the iOS share sheet. You choose the recipient and destination. The recipient or service manages the exported copy; deleting a record in STRATOS Voice does not delete that copy.</p>
<h2>Optional AI review</h2>
<p>Before sending, you see the exact text to be processed. Depending on the review, the app sends a selected passage or the current transcript with supporting output from two local models. <strong>AI review does not send audio or voice embeddings.</strong></p>
<p>With a personal or general enterprise connection, text is sent over HTTPS directly to the selected service. Settings and the review screen identify the service, server and model. Processing, further recipients and retention are determined by that provider or server operator. The publisher does not provide a shared API account; the service may charge the account owner.</p>
<p>With STRATOS, text passes through STRATOS to AKB. The current AKB integration uses OpenAI to propose corrections. Your organisational account and permissions control access. The service also processes account, revision and job identifiers required for review, result retrieval and operational audit. These are not used for advertising tracking.</p>
<p>A proposal does not automatically change a saved transcript. You explicitly accept changes into a new revision, preserving the original. AI may make mistakes and its proposals may differ from the original audio.</p>
<p>The organisation operating a STRATOS connection determines permissions, permitted content, retention and deletion of remote data, including backups. Contact its administrator for these rules and requests about remote data. AKB conditions do not apply to personal AI accounts or other enterprise servers.</p>
<h2>API keys, sign-in and organisational management</h2>
<p>You enter your personal API key in the app and can remove it or disconnect the service. It is stored in this iPhone’s Keychain, is not synchronised to iCloud and is excluded from ordinary exports and diagnostics. It is used only to authenticate to the selected server and is never sent to another connection. Saving a key does not send a transcript. Never send it to support; you can revoke it separately with the provider.</p>
<p>STRATOS sign-in uses your organisation’s secure page. STRATOS Voice does not store your password; iOS storage protects credentials used to renew sign-in. You can sign out in connection settings. Changing organisations separates sign-in and remote reviews while preserving local records.</p>
<p>On managed devices, an organisation may configure connections through MDM and restrict AI availability. MDM configuration does not itself start recording or send transcripts. Removing a managed app may delete local data under iOS and organisational rules.</p>
<h2>Diagnostics</h2>
<p>The app keeps a limited local history of operational states and errors without audio, transcript text, passwords or tokens. You explicitly share diagnostics with support. STRATOS Voice does not use advertising tracking. Apple’s own rules describe any diagnostics processed by its distribution platform.</p>
<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>Publisher: <strong>VCode</strong>. Privacy contact: <strong>podpora@zeleznalady.cz</strong>. Describe the service and data your request concerns; do not include recordings, transcripts or credentials. For data sent to an organisation, also contact the administrator of that STRATOS connection. Support must never request your password or access token.</p>
<p>Last updated: 7 October 2026.</p>
<h2>Support and the VCode website</h2>
<p>If you contact us, we use the information you choose to send to resolve your enquiry. We delete resolved support messages no later than 90 days after closure. The publisher cannot restore your local iPhone records from its own server. These pages are subject to the separate VCode website privacy policy; website analytics do not measure use of the iOS app.</p>
